   "text": "This is a cyclic undecapeptide in which a urea unit, \u2013N(Me)\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013, replaces one amide link. I traced the ring clockwise in the drawing (N\u2192C direction) and read each residue in turn:\n\n1. Ala, NH\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013C(=O)\n2. N\u2011Me\u2011Leu\n3. N\u2011Me\u2011Ser (CH2OH side chain)\n4. Val\n5. Urea linker: Val C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(Me), with no stereocentre\n6. Leu (its N carries the second urea N\u2011methyl)\n7. Val\n8. N\u2011Me\u2011Leu\n9. Leu\n10. Ala, drawn with a bold wedge on H\n11. N\u2011Me\u2011Leu, which closes the ring back onto the first Ala NH\n\nFor stereochemistry I assigned each \u03b1\u2011carbon from its hashed or wedged H and the arrangement of its N, C(=O) and side chain. Every residue comes out L except residue 10, whose bold wedge gives D\u2011Ala. The methyl and N bonds on that carbon are drawn close together, so this assignment is the least certain.\n\nSMILES: N1[C@@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)1"
